            <div xml:id="d919">

                <pb facs="0855" n="847" xml:id="pg847"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/10052: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-04-17T20:00:00+02:00">April 17, 1941—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 17—5:26 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1479. The German Ambassador to Turkey Von Papen is reported to have left Ankara
                    for Istanbul on his way to Berlin. A source which has wide connections in
                    official circles says this means the first step in endeavoring to force the
                    Turkish Government to come to terms and that high official circles are confident
                    of succeeding as a result of the altered military and strategic situation in the
                    Near East.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
